    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d854">

                <pb facs="1055" n="1047" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg1047"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">741.5314/2</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-02-19">February 19, 1938</date>.<lb/>[Received March
                        3.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to forward herewith, for
                    the information of the Treaty Division, five copies of the British White Paper
                    entitled “Treaty Series No. 14 (1938)—Exchanges of Notes Between His Majesty’s
                    Government in the United Kingdom and the Portuguese Government Regarding the
                    Boundary Between Tanganyika Territory and Mozambique: Lisbon, May 11, 1936, and
                    December 28, 1937”,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d854-f1"/> which have just been
                    received gratis from His Majesty’s Stationery Office.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herschel V.
                    Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
